  bootwright / diff
      Compare the context's desired state with what its apply realized, object by object.
      Without --observe it reads durable records only and contacts no host; with --observe it
      reads each realized block's target through that block's read-only observation. It changes
      nothing. It exits 0 whenever it renders a comparison; with --exit-code it exits 3 instead
      when any object differs or is unknown.

  Usage
    bootwright diff [flags]

  Command flags
      --exit-code  Exit 3 when any object differs or is unknown
      --observe    Read each realized block's target through its read-only observation

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  More detail
    Use --help --detail full to include SSH overrides.

  Examples
    bootwright diff --context lab --observe
